# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  First commit. Nothing is added before this file is.
#
#  git history is permanent: a restricted file committed once and deleted in the
#  next commit is still in the repository, still clonable, and still on GitHub.
#  Recovering from that means deleting the repository and starting again. So
#  the exclusions below are deliberately broader than the files that exist.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- restricted: borrower records and anything derived from them at cell level
*_ADM3_Year.csv
cluster_summary*
data_hybrid2*
dataset_for_modeling*
3_geo3y*
te_*.csv
TE_*.csv
*_predict.txt
metric_compare/
production_models/

# --- fitted model weights: trained on 1.5M individual credit histories
*.h5
*.keras
*.hdf5
*.model
*.pkl
*Keras*Model/
HBDL2*

# --- generated synthetic panel: too large for git, rebuild with make_synthetic.R
data/synthetic/panel_synthetic*.txt

# --- credentials and private cloud assets
*.json.key
service-account*.json
.Renviron
.env

# --- R and Python working files
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
.Rproj
renv/library/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
